Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> command
Rule 1     command -> action COORDINATE
Rule 2     command -> COMENZAR
Rule 3     command -> CAMBIO
Rule 4     action -> ATACAR
Rule 5     action -> DEFENDER
Rule 6     action -> ESCANEAR

Terminals, with rules where they appear

ATACAR               : 4
CAMBIO               : 3
COMENZAR             : 2
COORDINATE           : 1
DEFENDER             : 5
ESCANEAR             : 6
error                : 

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

action               : 1
command              : 0

Parsing method: LALR

state 0

    (0) S' -> . command
    (1) command -> . action COORDINATE
    (2) command -> . COMENZAR
    (3) command -> . CAMBIO
    (4) action -> . ATACAR
    (5) action -> . DEFENDER
    (6) action -> . ESCANEAR

    COMENZAR        shift and go to state 3
    CAMBIO          shift and go to state 4
    ATACAR          shift and go to state 5
    DEFENDER        shift and go to state 6
    ESCANEAR        shift and go to state 7

    command                        shift and go to state 1
    action                         shift and go to state 2

state 1

    (0) S' -> command .



state 2

    (1) command -> action . COORDINATE

    COORDINATE      shift and go to state 8


state 3

    (2) command -> COMENZAR .

    $end            reduce using rule 2 (command -> COMENZAR .)


state 4

    (3) command -> CAMBIO .

    $end            reduce using rule 3 (command -> CAMBIO .)


state 5

    (4) action -> ATACAR .

    COORDINATE      reduce using rule 4 (action -> ATACAR .)


state 6

    (5) action -> DEFENDER .

    COORDINATE      reduce using rule 5 (action -> DEFENDER .)


state 7

    (6) action -> ESCANEAR .

    COORDINATE      reduce using rule 6 (action -> ESCANEAR .)


state 8

    (1) command -> action COORDINATE .

    $end            reduce using rule 1 (command -> action COORDINATE .)

